        "detailed_description": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Hero Tactics is a love letter to oldschool tactics rpgs.</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Assemble a motley band of heroes and fight through gauntlet of battles to save the land from evil. Level-up your party, unlocking new skills and classes!</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Shrunk down for your convenience~</strong></h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Small Numbers: The units have roughly 2 to 5 health points. Your attacks will do 1 to 3 damage. All of the numbers are small enough to be easy to digest.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Micro Tactics: Each battle is held in a tiny 6x8 battlefield, letting each combat resolve quickly without a lot of turns wasted on moving into position.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Short Story: The campaign is composed of 5 to 8 chapters - you can probably play through the story in a single sitting.</p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Remastered for Steam</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >We released this project over half a decade ago as our first debut rpg. Back then, it had a much simpler design, and was missing a lot of quality-of-life features. So it has been long overdue for a remaster! Most notably, we completely overhauled every level to support a wider screen resolution.</p>",
        "about_the_game": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Hero Tactics is a love letter to oldschool tactics rpgs.</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Assemble a motley band of heroes and fight through gauntlet of battles to save the land from evil. Level-up your party, unlocking new skills and classes!</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Shrunk down for your convenience~</strong></h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Small Numbers: The units have roughly 2 to 5 health points. Your attacks will do 1 to 3 damage. All of the numbers are small enough to be easy to digest.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Micro Tactics: Each battle is held in a tiny 6x8 battlefield, letting each combat resolve quickly without a lot of turns wasted on moving into position.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Short Story: The campaign is composed of 5 to 8 chapters - you can probably play through the story in a single sitting.</p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Remastered for Steam</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >We released this project over half a decade ago as our first debut rpg. Back then, it had a much simpler design, and was missing a lot of quality-of-life features. So it has been long overdue for a remaster! Most notably, we completely overhauled every level to support a wider screen resolution.</p>",
